                "retweet_count": 5,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Today, I joined with other members of the Missouri Congressional Delegation in a letter to Governor Mike Kehoe, Missouri Department of Social Services Director Jessica Bax, and Missouri Department of Health and Senior Services Director Sarah Willson highlighting the Rural Health Transformation Program (RHTP) as a critical lifeline for rural Missouri and calling on officials to incorporate key policies in their application for RHTP resources.\n\nUnder the new tax cuts for working families law, the $50 billion RHTP was created to help expand access to care in rural communities. It will help improve the health and well-being of the nearly 60 million Americans that live in rural communities and support critical steps to address the rural health care crisis.",
                "text_lang": "en",
